        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Hypotenuse fixed at 10. SOH-CAH-TOA: \\(\\sin\\theta=\\text{opp}/10\\), \\(\\cos\\theta=\\text{adj}/10\\), \\(\\tan\\theta=\\text{opp}/\\text{adj}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Complex numbers</h3>A complex number has the form \\( a+bi \\) where \\( i=\\sqrt{-1} \\). Add by combining real and imaginary parts separately: \\( (3+2i)+(1-5i)=4-3i \\). Multiply using FOIL and replace \\( i^2 \\) with \\( -1 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Trigonometry & Complex Numbers",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "SOH-CAH-TOA: \\(\\sin\\theta = \\text{opp}/\\text{hyp}\\), \\(\\cos\\theta = \\text{adj}/\\text{hyp}\\), \\(\\tan\\theta = \\text{opp}/\\text{adj}\\). Pythagorean identity: \\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1\\). Exact values: \\(\\sin 30° = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\), \\(\\cos 30° = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\), \\(\\sin 45° = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\). Complex: \\(i^2 = -1\\); \\(|a+bi| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Finding all sides of a right triangle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "In right triangle, the hypotenuse is 13 and one angle is \\(22.6°\\). Find the other two sides. <p>Opposite \\(= 13\\sin 22.6° \\approx 13 \\times 0.3843 \\approx 5\\). Adjacent \\(= 13\\cos 22.6° \\approx 12\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sin^2\\theta}{1-\\cos\\theta}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Use \\(\\sin^2\\theta = 1-\\cos^2\\theta = (1-\\cos\\theta)(1+\\cos\\theta)\\). So \\(\\dfrac{(1-\\cos\\theta)(1+\\cos\\theta)}{1-\\cos\\theta} = 1+\\cos\\theta\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
